x86_64-linux  clang emits only the C2 variant of an *inline* constructor on this target and cxx1 emits C1 and C2, so cxx1 has _ZN3BoxI10HasDefaultEC1Ei and _ZN3BoxI9NoDefaultEC1Ev where clang has neither. A class template member is inline by nature and has no out-of-line form to move to, which is why this case cannot dodge it the way the plain classes above it do - they are written out of line for exactly that reason. The two are identical for a class with no virtual bases and both are mergeable definitions, so the extra C1 costs object size and nothing else. move-constructor.nonames and implicit-move.nonames record the same fact. Darwin and Windows agree on every name.
